  "unreadable": [],
  "notes": "Header callouts: dark boxes carry the silkscreen-style GPIO numbers (recorded first in functions), pink boxes the GPIO names (labels). UART JST: callout text 'GND 3V TX RX' with '(25)(24)' under TX and RX used as labels; board silkscreen GND/3V3/TXD/RXD recorded in functions. Qwiic labels from the inset (GPIO02/SDA, GPIO03/SCL); board silkscreen GND 3V3 SDA SCL. Battery JST-GH (only +/- marks), IPEX antenna, BOOT/IO00/Reset buttons skipped. LCD and BMU signal lists are not physical connectors.",
  "uncertain": [
    "USB connector identity: the metal receptacle at the bottom edge (under the battery JST) is unlabeled; it was treated as the USB connector, which sets bottom-first order for both headers and right-end-first order for the UART JST. If not USB, the headers would start at the top.",
    "uart-jst: the callout text 'GND 3V TX RX' and '(25)(24)' sits beside the connector rather than on leader lines; mapping each word to a pin in order (and (25) to TX, (24) to RX) is inferred."
  ]
